## 1. PROJECT BRIEF

- **Site name / brand:** **NAGAR-LEDGER // MBMC** (Mira-Bhayandar Public Works & Civic Accountability Ledger)[cite: 1]
- **What it is:** A real-time civic issue tracking, algorithmic prioritization, and public SLA accountability web application for citizens and ward officers of Mira-Bhayandar (Wards 1–24)[cite: 1]. It replaces opaque, manual paper/portal complaints with a transparent, tamper-evident public works ledger.
- **Target audience:**
  1. **Everyday residents & commuters of Mira-Bhayandar** (ages 18–68, predominantly mobile users on 4G/5G Android devices commuting via Mira Road & Bhayandar railway stations or Western Express Highway) who want to report garbage overflow, water leaks, or road damage in under 30 seconds without bureaucratic friction and see proof of resolution[cite: 1].
  2. **Local citizen groups, housing society secretaries (CHSs), and journalists** tracking ward-level SLA compliance across localities like Kashimira, Golden Nest, Shivar Garden, Naya Nagar, Navghar, Bhayandar West, and Uttan[cite: 1].
  3. **MBMC Junior Engineers, Sanitary Inspectors, and Ward Officers** who need a prioritized dispatch queue ranked by civic urgency rather than political noise[cite: 1].
- **Primary goal (one only):** Get citizens to **log a geo-verified civic complaint (or "+1 Confirm" an existing nearby report) in under 30 seconds** and immediately receive a live, trackable SLA ticket[cite: 1].
- **Secondary goals:**
  1. Expose real-time ward-by-ward performance (Mean Time to Resolve, SLA breach rates, and active backlogs) to enforce public transparency[cite: 1].
  2. Prevent premature "fake closures" by requiring geo-tagged "After" photos and a 48-hour Citizen Verification window[cite: 1].
  3. Demonstrate how the transparent **Civic Priority Score (CPS)** ranks issues objectively based on severity, proximity to critical infrastructure, citizen upvotes, and SLA decay[cite: 1].
- **Tone / personality:** **Swiss Municipal Utilitarian & Editorial Ledger** — authoritative, crisp, civic-minded, transparent, and unpretentious[cite: 1]. Think a classic physical municipal dispatch logbook crossed with modern high-density data journalism (`gov.uk` clarity + `linear.app` speed + `usgraphics.com` tabular discipline). Zero startup fluff, zero bureaucratic obfuscation.
- **Reference sites I admire:**
  1. `https://www.gov.uk` — Brutally clear typography, high-contrast focus states, zero decorative bloat, and immediate task orientation[cite: 1].
  2. `https://usgraphics.com` — Exposed 1px hairline grids, technical monospace metadata, archival paper-and-ink warmth, and strict tabular alignment[cite: 1].
  3. `https://linear.app` — Keyboard-first speed, crisp status badges, subtle state transitions, and high-signal issue tracking without visual clutter[cite: 1].
- **Things to avoid:**
  - Startup SaaS clichés ("Revolutionizing Smart Cities", "Empowering Citizens")[cite: 1].
  - Fake 3D city illustrations, glowing purple/blue gradients, floating glassmorphism cards, or cartoon avatars[cite: 1].
  - Requiring a complex account registration wall before a citizen can report a burst water pipe or pothole[cite: 1].
  - Hiding data behind vague percentages; always show exact ticket counts, ward numbers, timestamps, and street names[cite: 1].
- **Pages / Views needed (Single-Page App or Multi-Route with clean URLs):**
  1. **Home / Live Dispatch Ledger (`/`)**: Hero with instant "Report in 30s" trigger + Live Ticker of recent MBMC ward actions + Interactive Public Issue Ledger (filterable by Ward, Category, Status, and Priority Score) + Algorithmic Priority Score Explainer + Before/After Citizen Audit showcase[cite: 1].
  2. **30-Second Report & Duplicate-Check Flow (`/report` or full-height accessible Drawer/View)**: Step-by-step zero-friction intake with simulated GPS/EXIF auto-detection for Mira-Bhayandar landmarks, automatic 50m duplicate detection ("3 neighbors already reported this pothole at Golden Nest Circle — +1 Confirm instead?"), severity selector, and instant Ticket ID generation[cite: 1].
  3. **Ward Accountability Scorecard (`/wards`)**: Comparative ledger of MBMC Prabhags/Wards (Mira Road East, Kashimira, Bhayandar West, Bhayandar East, Navghar, Uttan) showing MTTR (hours), SLA Compliance %, Open Critical Issues, and Escalated Tickets[cite: 1].
  4. **Ticket Inspector & Escalation Timeline (`/ticket/:id`)**: Deep-dive view of a specific complaint showing the immutable audit trail (`Logged` -> `Clustered` -> `Assigned to Ward Officer` -> `Work Crew Dispatched` -> `After-Photo Uploaded` -> `Citizen Verified`), live SLA countdown timer, and the Priority Score breakdown formula[cite: 1].
  5. **Custom 404 Page (`/404`)**: Styled as a "Missing Municipal Record / Unindexed Ward Route" with instant navigation back to the live ledger[cite: 1].
- **Real content & unique solution features to implement (build with realistic, stateful Mira-Bhayandar data in `/src/data/`):**
  1. **Algorithmic Civic Priority Score (CPS 0–100)**: Every issue displays a transparent, inspectable score calculated from:
     - *Base Category Urgency* (Water Main Leak: 35, Open Manhole/Road Cave-in: 40, Uncollected Garbage >48h: 25, Pothole: 20).
     - *Community Verification Cluster* (`+3 pts` per unique neighbor confirmation within a 50-meter radius, capped at +25).
     - *Critical Zone Multiplier* (`1.25x` if within 200m of a school, hospital, railway station like Mira Road/Bhayandar Station, or flood-prone nullah).
     - *SLA Decay Boost* (`+1 pt` for every 4 hours past the initial inspection window).
  2. **50-Meter Geo-Deduplication ("+1 Confirm" Engine)**: When a user selects a locality (e.g., *Shivar Garden, Mira Road East* or *Station Road, Bhayandar West*) and category in the Report flow, dynamically show matching active tickets nearby so the user can add weight (`+1 Confirm & Subscribe to SMS Alerts`) instead of creating a duplicate ticket.
  3. **Automated SLA Escalation Matrix**: Each category has a strict statutory SLA (Water Leak: 24h, Garbage Overflow: 12h, Road Damage/Pothole: 72h). Display a live `tabular-nums` countdown on open tickets. When an SLA breaches (`< 00h 00m`), the UI automatically flags the status as `SLA BREACHED — ESCALATED TO DMC` with the assigned official's designation.
  4. **Citizen Proof-of-Fix Audit (Before/After Split View)**: Resolved tickets cannot bypass citizen scrutiny. Include an interactive, keyboard-accessible Before/After visual comparison component showing timestamped, geo-matched inspection photos where residents can click **"Verify Fix"** or **"Re-open (Fix Incomplete)"**.
  5. **Multilingual Micro-Toggle (`EN` / `मराठी` / `हिंदी`)**: Provide a lightweight language switcher in the header that translates key navigation, primary CTA labels, and civic categories (e.g., *कचरा संकलन / पाणी गळती / रस्ते दुरुस्ती*) so the tool feels authentically built for Maharashtra's civic context.
- **Tech stack:** **Vite + React + TypeScript + plain CSS with custom properties** (no Tailwind, no UI component libraries, inline SVG icons via Lucide or custom crisp 1.5px stroke SVGs)[cite: 1]. Persist user-submitted reports and "+1 Confirmations" in `localStorage` (with `try/catch` guards) so the app works as a fully functional interactive prototype[cite: 1].
- **Deploy target:** **Vercel / Netlify** (configure clean SPA routing fallback)[cite: 1].

