## 2. THE "NOT-AI" RULES (most important section)

AI-generated sites share recognizable tells[cite: 1]. You must avoid ALL of these[cite: 1]:

**Visual tells to ban**
- Purple-to-blue / pink-to-orange gradient hero backgrounds and gradient text on every heading[cite: 1]
- Generic glassmorphism cards floating on blurry blobs[cite: 1]
- Three identical rounded cards in a row with an emoji or icon on top, as the default content block[cite: 1]
- Emoji used as icons or bullet decoration[cite: 1]
- Every section centered, same width, same padding, same rhythm[cite: 1]
- Huge soft drop shadows on everything; border-radius 16-24px on everything[cite: 1]
- Stock "abstract 3D shapes" or generic gradient orbs[cite: 1]
- Neon glows, excessive sparkles, "✨" anywhere[cite: 1]
- Identical hover effect (scale 1.05 + shadow) on every element[cite: 1]

**Copy tells to ban**
- "Unleash", "Elevate", "Seamless", "Revolutionize", "Empower", "Cutting-edge", "Next-gen", "In today's fast-paced world", "Your all-in-one solution", "Take your X to the next level"[cite: 1]
- Headlines that are two buzzwords joined by "&"[cite: 1]
- Perfectly parallel 3-bullet lists with matching word counts in every section[cite: 1]
- Em-dash-heavy, over-polished marketing sentences. Write like a sharp human: specific, concrete, slightly opinionated, with real numbers and nouns[cite: 1]

**Structural tells to ban**
- Lorem ipsum (write real placeholder copy instead)[cite: 1]
- Fake testimonials with fake names and stock avatars. If no real ones exist, omit the section or use a clearly labeled placeholder[cite: 1]
- "Trusted by" logo strips with invented companies[cite: 1]

**What human-made sites actually do (do these)**
- Commit to ONE strong visual idea and repeat it with discipline (for NAGAR-LEDGER: **an exposed 1px architectural blueprint/ledger grid with stamped ticket serial numbers, live tabular-nums SLA clocks, and high-contrast municipal status tags**)[cite: 1]
- Use **asymmetry and varied rhythm**: some sections left-aligned, some full-bleed, some split, some dense, some airy[cite: 1]
- Use **real typographic contrast**: scale jumps, weight contrast, tight tracking on large display text, comfortable leading on body text[cite: 1]
- Use a **restrained palette**: 1 neutral family (warm archival newsprint/stone in light mode; carbon asphalt in dark mode) + 1 primary accent (Municipal Signal Vermilion `#D9381E`) + semantic status tokens (SLA Verified Green, Escalation Amber), with accessible contrast[cite: 1]
- Add **small crafted details**: custom selection color, styled focus rings, a considered favicon, custom 404, subtle grain or hairline borders, thoughtful cursor or link underline treatment, careful footer[cite: 1]
- Make motion purposeful and quiet (it explains or rewards, never decorates)[cite: 1]
- Prefer hairlines (1px borders), whitespace, and type over boxes and shadows[cite: 1]

