## 3. DESIGN SYSTEM (build this FIRST, as CSS custom properties)

Create `styles/tokens.css` before any component[cite: 1].

### 3.1 Color
- Define semantic tokens, not just raw colors: `--bg`, `--bg-elevated`, `--surface`, `--text`, `--text-muted`, `--border`, `--accent`, `--accent-hover`, `--accent-contrast`, `--success`, `--warning`, `--danger`, `--focus-ring`[cite: 1]
- Build a 9-step neutral scale (warm stone/newsprint `#FAF8F5` to `#111315`) and a 9-step accent scale (Civic Signal Vermilion `#D9381E` in light mode, `#FF5A3D` in dark mode)[cite: 1]
- Pick colors that fit the brand personality. Justify the palette in a short comment[cite: 1]
- Provide **light and dark themes** via `prefers-color-scheme` plus a manual toggle that persists in `localStorage` (guard with try/catch)[cite: 1]. Avoid a flash of wrong theme by setting the theme attribute in an inline script in `<head>`[cite: 1]
- Text contrast must meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large text and UI components). Verify, don't assume[cite: 1]

### 3.2 Typography
- Choose **a deliberate font pairing** (max two main families + monospace for ledger data): e.g., **Space Grotesk** or **Plus Jakarta Sans** for crisp architectural headings/body + **JetBrains Mono** or **IBM Plex Mono** for ticket IDs (`MBMC-2026-0842`), ward codes, GPS coordinates, and SLA countdowns[cite: 1]. Avoid defaulting to Inter/Roboto/Poppins for everything[cite: 1]
- Use `font-display: swap`, preload the critical font file, subset if possible[cite: 1]
- Fluid type scale with `clamp()`: e.g. body `clamp(1rem, 0.95rem + 0.25vw, 1.125rem)`, h1 `clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 5vw, 5.5rem)`[cite: 1]. Use a consistent ratio (1.2-1.333)[cite: 1]
- Body line-height 1.5-1.7; headings 1.05-1.2; large display text gets negative letter-spacing (-0.02em to -0.04em)[cite: 1]
- Measure: paragraphs max `65ch`[cite: 1]
- `text-wrap: balance` on headings, `text-wrap: pretty` on paragraphs[cite: 1]
- Enable `font-feature-settings` / `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` where numbers align (especially SLA timers, Priority Scores, and Ward tables)[cite: 1]

### 3.3 Spacing and layout
- 4px base unit; spacing tokens `--space-1` ... `--space-12` (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 160, 192)[cite: 1]
- Section vertical padding fluid: `clamp(4rem, 8vw, 9rem)`[cite: 1]
- 12-column grid on desktop, 8 on tablet, 4 on mobile, with a max content width (~1240px) and a narrower reading width for text[cite: 1]
- Use CSS Grid for page layout and Flexbox for component internals. Use `gap`, never margin hacks[cite: 1]
- Break the grid on purpose in 1-2 places (e.g., an oversized full-bleed Ward Ledger ticker or an overlapping live SLA inspection card) for personality[cite: 1]

### 3.4 Shape, depth, borders
- Choose ONE radius system: **2px sharp architectural corners** (`--radius-sm: 2px`, `--radius-md: 4px`, `--radius-pill: 999px` strictly for status tags) and apply consistently[cite: 1]
- Elevation: max 3 shadow levels, subtle, layered (two-part shadows look more real than one big blur)[cite: 1]
- Prefer 1px borders using `--border` over heavy shadows[cite: 1]

### 3.5 Motion
- Tokens: `--ease-out: cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)`, `--ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1)`, durations 150ms / 250ms / 500ms[cite: 1]
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. No layout-thrashing animations[cite: 1]
- Scroll reveals: subtle (8-16px translate + fade), staggered by 50-80ms, triggered once via `IntersectionObserver`[cite: 1]
- **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`**: disable parallax, auto-play, large movements; keep only opacity fades[cite: 1]
- No animation longer than 600ms for UI feedback[cite: 1]

### 3.6 Iconography and imagery
- One icon set, consistent stroke weight (e.g. Lucide or custom 1.5px technical inline SVG). No emoji icons[cite: 1]
- Images: build high-craft **SVG technical diagrams / architectural before-and-after street schematics / ward boundary vector maps of Mira-Bhayandar** (showing Mira Creek, Western Express Highway, Railway Line, and Wards 1–24) rather than generic stock photos[cite: 1]
- All images/SVGs: explicit `width`/`height` (prevents layout shift), `loading="lazy"` below the fold, `decoding="async"`, meaningful `alt` text (or `alt=""` if decorative)[cite: 1]
- Use `aspect-ratio` and `object-fit` deliberately[cite: 1]

