## 6. ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.2 AA minimum)

- Semantic HTML first: `<header> <nav> <main> <section> <article> <aside> <footer>`, one `<h1>`, logical heading order, landmarks labeled[cite: 1]
- "Skip to content" link as the first focusable element[cite: 1]
- Fully keyboard operable, logical tab order, **visible `:focus-visible` ring** designed to match the brand (never `outline: none` without replacement)[cite: 1]
- ARIA only when native HTML can't do it. Correct `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, `aria-current`, `aria-live="polite"` for dynamic filter counts, "+1 Confirm" increments, and form submission feedback[cite: 1]
- Color is never the only signal (pair SLA status colors with explicit status icons and text labels like `[SLA BREACH]`, `[IN PROGRESS]`, `[VERIFIED]`); sufficient contrast; support `prefers-contrast` and `forced-colors` where reasonable[cite: 1]
- Alt text, `<label>` for every input, `lang` attribute on `<html>`[cite: 1]
- Modals/drawers (Issue Reporter & Ticket Inspector): focus trap, return focus on close, ESC closes, `inert` on background[cite: 1]
- Target size, no drag-only interactions (ensure Before/After audit slider works via keyboard arrow keys or buttons as well as pointer), no motion that can't be paused. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`[cite: 1]
- Run axe or Lighthouse accessibility audit and fix to **score 100** or document exceptions[cite: 1]

